// {2} sorcery: "draw a card. Improvise." Pins the ARTIFACT arm of the per-pip
// alternative-payment hook (PayPips): improvise lets a generic pip be paid by
// tapping an untapped artifact you control ([CR#702.126a]) — "rather than pay
// that mana", without lowering the {2} mana value ([CR#202.3,702.51b]). Convoke
// and delve exercise the creature-tap and graveyard-exile arms; this minimal
// {2} twin isolates the artifact-tap arm for a small, deterministic engine
// test. No real improvise spell whose non-cost effect ("draw a card") is this
// minimal is canonized yet. Per plugins/testing/README.md, canonize a real
// improvise spell and delete this once one lands.
//
// The improvise static is spelled DIRECTLY as a `PayPips` row (the keyword
// macro sugar is exercised on the keyword layer) so the engine test does not
// depend on the keyword layer.
Normal(
    name: "Sorcery Improvise Draw",
    mana_cost: [Generic(2)],
    types: [Sorcery],
    abilities: [
        Spell(effect: Draw(1)),
        Static(PayPips(Generic, TapToPay(And([Type(Artifact), ControlledBy(Ref(You))])))),
    ],
)
